# Her reaction to your answer. {move} what you did, {fit} good/neutral/bad (how well it landed), {step} 1-3.
# A rule with "opens" carries the talk to a next step (up to 3) with those answers; without it, the topic ends here.
# 2026-10-27: every rule has 4+ lines (each "- " line counts apart in the "said lately" memory, so one line with
# alternatives repeats much sooner than four lines), and every move has its own neutral answer.

# ================= generic by fit =================
@rule react.good
on react
when fit=good
feel smile
- [Ehehe... yeah.|You always know what to say.|I'm glad I talked to you.|Thanks. Really.]
- [That's sweet of you.|Mm. I like talking with you.|You get me, huh?]
- [See, this is why I like talking to you.|Okay, you just made my day a little better.|Heh. Yeah. Exactly that.]
- [I didn't expect that from you. In a good way.|You're easy to talk to, you know?|Hehe. Good answer.]
- [Not many people get what I mean about {like}.|I knew you'd understand about {like}.] [You do, though.|That's why I told you.]
- [I should tell {who} what you just said.|{Who} wouldn't have put it like that.] [Hehe.|You're better at this.]

@rule react.good.onday
on react
when fit=good kind=day
feel smile
- [Talking about {mything} with you is easy.|I wasn't planning to talk about {mything} today.] [I'm glad I did.|It helps, somehow.]
- [Most people would've changed the subject from {mything} by now.|Nobody else wants to hear about {mything}.] [You actually listen.|So, thanks.]
- [Funny, {mything} doesn't feel so heavy now.|You make {mything} sound better than it is.] [Hehe.|Keep talking.]

@rule react.neutral
on react
when fit=neutral
- [Hm. Maybe.|I guess so.|Mm, could be.|Okay.]
- [If you say so.|Hm, fair enough.|Huh. I hadn't thought of it like that.]
- [I don't know. Maybe you're right.|That's one way to see it.|Mm... I'll take your word for it.]
- [Heh. Okay, sure.|Hm, I'll think about that.|Yeah, maybe.] [Anyway.|Where was I?|]
- [Not sure {who} would agree.|Hm, {who} would have a different answer.] [But okay.|Maybe.]
- [I'm not sure that's how it works with {like}.|Hm, {like} isn't for everyone.] [But okay.|Fair enough.]

@rule react.neutral.onday
on react
when fit=neutral kind=day
- [Hm, I hadn't looked at {mything} that way.|That's one way to look at {mything}.] [I guess.|Maybe.]
- [I don't know what to think about {mything}.|Mm, {mything}...] [Ask me another day.|We'll see.]
- [Well, {mything} is what it is.|{Mything} won't change either way.] [Right?|So, yeah.]

@rule react.bad
on react
when fit=bad
feel pout
- [...Right.|That's not really what I wanted to hear.|Wow. Okay.|Hmph.]
- [Seriously?|Was that supposed to help?|Um. No.]
- [You really don't get it, huh.|...Never mind.|Forget I said anything.]
- [That's not funny.|Not the time.|Ugh, you sound like my brother.] [Let's just drop it.|Whatever.|]
- [Don't talk about {who} like you know everything.|You'd better not say that in front of {who}.]
- [If you don't care about {like}, just say so.|You don't have to fake an interest in {like}.]

# ================= ask =================

@rule react.bad.onday
on react
when fit=bad kind=day
feel pout
- [I wanted to talk about {mything}, not that.|That has nothing to do with {mything}.] [Forget it.|Never mind.]
- [You weren't really listening about {mything}, were you?|Did you hear anything I said about {mything}?] [Great.|Wow.]
- [That's the last time I bring up {mything} with you.|I knew I shouldn't have mentioned {mything}.]

@rule react.ask.good.go
on react
when kind=confide hurt=yes move=ask fit=good step<=2
opens comfort,share,invite
- [Well... since you asked.|Okay, so here's the thing.|You really want to know?] [It's been building up for a while.|I haven't told anyone this.|It's kind of a long story.]
- [Honestly?|Promise you won't laugh?|Okay, but this stays between us.] [It's been on my mind all day.|I keep going back and forth about it.]
- [You're actually curious? Huh.|Nobody ever asks me that.] [So... it's like this.|Okay, here goes.]
- [Ah, where do I start...|Hmm. Let me think how to put it.] [It's more complicated than it looks.|It's silly, but it matters to me.]
- [Well, {who} was part of it.|It has to do with {who}, actually.] [I don't know if I should say.|You know how that goes.]
- [With {like}, it's a whole thing.|Nobody ever asks me about {like}.] [There's a story behind it.|I'll tell you how it started.]
- [The {club} has a lot to do with it.|It all goes back to the {club}.] [Okay, so...|You really want the whole story?]

@rule react.ask.good.go.onday
on react
when kind=confide hurt=yes move=ask fit=good step<=2
opens comfort,share,invite
- [Okay, {mything}.|So, about {mything}...] [It started small and then it got out of hand.|There's a part I didn't tell you.|It's not what it looks like from outside.]
- [You want the real answer about {mything}?|Since you asked about {mything}...] [I've been thinking about it more than I should.|It matters more than I let on.]

@rule react.ask.good
on react
when move=ask fit=good
feel smile
- [Thanks for asking. Most people don't.|It feels good to say it out loud.|You're a good listener, you know that?]
- [I didn't think anyone noticed.|You're sweet for asking.|Talking about it helps, actually.]
- [Okay, that's the whole story.|And that's it! Thanks for listening.|Phew. Glad I got that out.]
- [You really pay attention, huh?|Not many people care enough to ask.|Mm. I'm glad it was you who asked.]
- [Now you know what I see in {like}.|That's why I can't stop with {like}.] [Thanks for asking.|Don't laugh.]
- [Don't tell {who} I said all that.|Ask {who} and you'd get a different story.] [Thanks for listening.|But that's my side.]

@rule react.ask.good.onday
on react
when move=ask fit=good kind=day
feel smile
- [That's all there is to {mything}, really.|So that's {mything}.] [Thanks for hearing me out.|You didn't even yawn.]
- [I've never told anyone that much about {mything}.|You got more out of me about {mything} than most people do.] [You're good at this.|Hehe.]
- [You remember stuff like {mything}, don't you?|You really do pay attention to {mything}.] [I like that.|Nobody else does.]

@rule react.ask.neutral
on react
when move=ask fit=neutral
- [There's not much more to it.|That's about it, really.|I don't know what else to say.]
- [It's not that interesting.|Eh, it's nothing special.|You're not missing much.]
- [I'd rather not get into it.|Maybe another time.|It's a long story. Some other day.]
- [Hm. Hard to explain.|You had to be there.|It is what it is.]
- [You should ask {who} instead.|{Who} would tell it better.] [I only know my side.|I wasn't paying attention.]
- [There's not much to say about {like}.|I can't really explain {like}.] [I just like what I like.|You either get it or you don't.]

@rule react.ask.neutral.onday
on react
when move=ask fit=neutral kind=day
- [Honestly, there isn't much to {mything}.|{Mything} isn't as interesting as it sounds.] [Sorry.|That's all I've got.]
- [What else do you want to know about {mything}?|I already said what I think about {mything}.]
- [I'd have to think about {mything} a bit more.|I can't really explain {mything}.] [Maybe later.|You know?]

@rule react.ask.bad
on react
when move=ask fit=bad
feel pout
- [Why do you want to know so badly?|That's kind of personal.|Let's not.]
- [You're nosy today.|Do I ask about your business?|That's none of your concern.]
- [I don't really want to talk about it.|Can we not?|Drop it, please.]
- [Who are you, the university paper?|Are you writing a report on me?|Interrogation over.]
- [Did {who} send you to ask?|Go ask {who} if you're that curious.]
- [Do you even care about {like}, or are you just being nosy?|Why are you so interested in {like} all of a sudden?]

@rule react.ask.bad.onday
on react
when move=ask fit=bad kind=day
feel pout
- [Why are you digging into {mything}?|What's it to you, {mything}?] [Drop it.|Seriously.]
- [I said what I wanted to say about {mything}.|{Mything} is my business.] [That's enough.|Leave it.]
- [Stop asking about {mything}.|Enough about {mything}.] [You're making it worse.|Please.]

@rule react.ask.day.low
on react
when move=ask kind=day low=yes fit=good step<=1
opens comfort,invite,share
feel sad
- [It's just... {mything}.|I don't know. Everything at once.] [I keep messing up.|I feel like nobody notices.|I'm tired of pretending I'm fine.]
- [It's stupid, really.|You'll think it's silly.] [{Mything} is getting to me.|I just feel off today.]
- [I didn't sleep well, and then {mything}...|It's been one of those days.] [I just want it to be over.|Nothing's going right.]
- [Can I be honest?|Promise not to laugh.] [I feel kind of alone lately.|I'm worried about {mything}.|I'm just tired.]
- [I keep telling everyone it's nothing.|I didn't want to say it.] [But {mything} has been on me all day.|It's {mything}, and I can't shake it.]
- [Since this morning, it's been {mything}.|It started with {mything}.] [One thing after another.|And nobody noticed.]
- {student}[I smile in class, and all the while it's {mything}.|You're the first to ask about {mything}.] [I'm tired.|Thanks.]
- [{Who} has a lot to do with it.|Part of it is {who}.] [I don't want to make it a big thing.|It's complicated.]
- [The {club} isn't helping either.|Even at the {club} I couldn't stop thinking about it.] [I just need a break.|Sorry.]

@rule react.ask.day.good
on react
when move=ask kind=day mood=cheerful fit=good|neutral step<=1
opens tease,praise,invite
feel laugh
- {student}[Nothing big! I just woke up happy.|Okay, okay. I got a letter from an old friend.|The professor praised my assignments in front of everyone!]
- [I found money in my old coat!|My favorite song came on right when I woke up.|The bakery had my favorite bread!]
- [Secret~ ...Okay, fine, I slept really well.|I finally finished something I've been working on!]
- [It's just a good day, you know?|Everything's going my way today.|I got a message that made me smile.]
- [You really want to know why I'm in such a good mood?|Why am I smiling?] [Everything just clicked this morning.|Because nothing went wrong all day.]
- [Even the walk to campus was nice.|The first class flew by.] [Days like this are rare!|I can't explain it!]
- [Good things come in threes, and I've had two.|I've been lucky all day.] [I'm waiting for the third.|Maybe you're next.]
- [The {club} went great.|Everything went right at the {club}.] [Can you tell?|I'm still on a high.]
- [I had some {fav} and that was enough.|You know what did it? {Fav}.] [I'm easy to please.|Don't laugh.]

@rule react.ask.gossip
on react
when move=ask kind=gossip fit=good|neutral step<=1
opens agree,defend,tease
- [From what I heard, it started {when}.|Apparently it's been going on for a while.|{Who} told someone, who told someone...] [Now everyone knows.|It just spiraled from there.]
- [Well, I didn't see it myself.|I heard it in the hallway.] [But people are sure about it.|Half the class is talking.]
- [Okay, so, {deed}.|Get this: {deed}.] [Can you believe it?|I almost didn't.]
- [I'm not saying it's true...|Don't quote me on this.] [But it sounded pretty real.|It's all anyone talks about.]
- [So {who} and the whole thing started {when}.|It was {when}, and {who} was right in the middle of it.] [Nobody saw it coming.|It got around fast.]
- [What I know is, {deed}.|All I can tell you is that {deed}.] [The rest is guesswork.|Anything else is rumor.]
- [{Src} told me, and {src} doesn't usually lie.|I got it from {src}.] [Make of it what you want.|That's all I know.]
- [Ask {who} and you'd hear something else.|{Who} would deny it, of course.] [But I know what I heard.|But still.]
- [The how isn't the strange part.|The details keep changing.] [It's why {who} did it.|What I can't figure out is {who}.]

@rule react.ask.you.saw
on react
when move=ask kind=you how=witness step<=1
opens admit,hush,comfort
feel worried
- [I just... I didn't expect it from you.|I don't know how I feel about it.|I saw enough.] [What do you want me to say?|I keep thinking about it.]
- [I was right there, you know.|It's not like I was looking for it.] [It was hard to unsee.|I didn't know what to do.]
- [I won't pretend I didn't see it.|It surprised me, that's all.] [Is that who you are?|I'm still processing.]
- [Honestly? It was a lot.|I wasn't expecting that.] [I just want to understand.|Why there, of all places?]
- [I saw it {when}.|It was {when}, and I was right there.] [You didn't notice me.|I couldn't look away in time.]
- [I don't know how to look at you after that.|It changed how I see you, a little.] [Say something.|I'm not sure if that's bad.]

@rule react.ask.you.saw.onday
on react
when move=ask kind=you how=witness step<=1
opens admit,hush,comfort
feel worried
- [I keep thinking about {mything}.|I know what I saw, about {mything}.] [I can't just forget it.|Tell me what that was.]
- [I wasn't spying.|Don't think I went looking for it.] [You weren't exactly hiding {mything}.|It was right in front of me.]
- [I haven't told anyone about {mything}.|So far I've kept {mything} to myself.] [Yet.|But I want to know why.]

@rule react.ask.you.heard
on react
when move=ask kind=you how=heard|rumor
opens correct,deny,admit
- [{Src} told me.|I heard it from {src}.|Everyone, honestly.] [Half the class knows by now.|I didn't go looking for it.]
- [It's going around.|You can't keep things quiet here.] [I heard it twice today.|Even the first years know.]
- {student}[Someone in my class was talking about it.|I overheard it.] [I didn't want to believe it.|Is it true?]
- [Does it matter who?|Let's just say a few people.] [What matters is if it's true.|So, is it?]
- [What I heard is that {deed}.|The story going around is that {deed}.] [So?|Is that right?]
- [{Src} heard it first, I think.|I got it from {src}, who got it from somewhere else.] [It's all over the class.|You know how it is.]
- [It came up {when}.|It's been going around since {when}.] [I didn't start it.|I just listened.]
- [Nobody's hiding it.|It's not exactly a secret.] [If it's not true, say so.|Is it true or not?]
- [Why do you care who said it?|Who said it isn't the point.] [Did you do it?|Just tell me.]

@rule react.ask.us
on react
when move=ask kind=us fit=good step<=1
opens share,tease,invite
feel shy
- [How I felt? ...Happy. Really happy.|Honestly? My heart was racing the whole time.|I didn't want it to end.]
- [I keep thinking about it.|I smile every time I remember.] [Is that weird?|Don't laugh.]
- [It was nice. Really nice.|It felt... right, you know?] [I hope you felt it too.|We should do it again.]
- [D-don't make me say it.|You know how I felt.] [...Good. Very good.|It was the best part of my week.]
- [It happened {when}, and I still get nervous.|That was only {when}?] [It feels longer.|My face gets hot.]

@rule react.ask.us.onday
on react
when move=ask kind=us fit=good step<=1
opens share,tease,invite
feel shy
- [{Mything}? I think about it more than I'd admit.|How did {mything} feel?] [Warm.|Like I could stop being careful.]
- {student}[I went home and thought about {mything} all night.|I replayed {mything} in class.] [The professor had to call me twice.|Don't tell anyone.]
- [The best part of {mything}?|What I liked most about {mything}?] [That it was you.|You don't know?]
- [I was scared you didn't feel the same about {mything}.|Tell me {mything} meant something to you too.] [So I'm glad you asked.|Please.]

@rule react.ask.like
on react
when move=ask likes=yes fit=good step<=1
opens share,invite,praise
feel laugh
- [Oh, where do I even start?|Okay, you asked for it.] [It started when I was little.|It just makes me happy.|I could show you sometime.]
- [You really want to hear about {like}?|Careful, I could go on for hours.] [It's the best thing ever.|It's how I relax.]
- [Okay, so, {like}...|Ah, {like}! My favorite.] [It never gets old.|Nobody gets it like I do.]
- [I don't know, I just love it.|It's hard to explain.] [You'd have to try it with me.|It makes everything better.]
- [With {like}, the first time got me hooked.|What got me into {like}?] [I was a kid, and I never let go.|I can still remember the day.]
- [The best part of {like} is that it's just for me.|What I love about {like} is how quiet my head gets.] [You know?|Weird, right?]
- [Nobody's ever asked me about {like} like that.|Most people roll their eyes at {like}.] [You really are curious.|But not you.]
- [I could show you what I mean about {like}.|If you want, we can {likedo} sometime.] [It's better than hearing me talk.|Just saying.]
- [My favorite thing about {like}? There are too many.|You want my top three of {like}?] [I'd need all lunch break.|Sit down.]

# ================= comfort =================
@rule react.comfort.good
on react
when move=comfort fit=good
feel smile
- [...Thanks. I needed that.|You're really kind, you know.|I feel a little better already.|Hearing that from you helps.]
- [Okay. Yeah. You're right.|I'll be fine. Thanks to you.|Mm. I think I can breathe again.]
- [You always know what to say.|I didn't think talking would help, but it did.|Sorry for being gloomy.]
- [Can you stay a bit longer?|You're a good friend.|I'll remember this.]
- [I'll stop worrying about {who} for now.|Maybe {who} and I will be okay.] [Because you said so.|Thanks.]
- [I can go back to the {club} now.|I think I can face the {club}.] [I needed that first.|Thank you.]

@rule react.comfort.good.onday
on react
when move=comfort fit=good kind=day
feel smile
- [I needed someone to say that about {mything}.|{Mything} felt so big until you said that.] [Thanks.|I can breathe now.]
- [I've been carrying {mything} around all day.|Nobody's said anything about {mything} until you.] [It's lighter now.|Thanks for noticing.]
- [You didn't even try to fix {mything}.|You didn't tell me {mything} was silly.] [That's why it helped.|That means a lot.]

@rule react.comfort.good.go
on react
when move=comfort fit=good step<=1 low=yes
opens invite,share,tease
feel smile
- [Okay. Okay, I'll be fine.|You're right. I'm overthinking it.] [Can you stay a little longer?|Distract me with something?]
- [Thanks. Really.|I feel lighter already.] [Tell me something fun?|Talk about something else with me?]
- [Mm... I needed to hear that.|You're good at this.] [What about you? How's your day?|Stay with me a bit?]
- [I think I'll survive.|It's not the end of the world, right?] [Got any plans later?|Cheer me up some more?]
- [Maybe I'll talk to {who} later.|{Who} can wait till tomorrow.] [What are you doing after this?|Keep me company till then?]
- [I don't feel like going to the {club} yet.|The {club} can manage without me for a minute.] [Talk to me a bit more?|Stay?]

@rule react.comfort.good.go.onday
on react
when move=comfort fit=good step<=1 low=yes kind=day
opens invite,share,tease
feel smile
- [Okay, enough about {mything}.|{Mything} can wait a little.] [Tell me something nice?|What about you?]
- [I think I needed to stop thinking about {mything}.|You got me out of my head about {mything}.] [Stay a bit?|Now what?]
- [I won't let {mything} ruin the whole day.|{Mything} isn't the end of the world, is it?] [Got any ideas?|Help me forget it?]

@rule react.comfort.neutral
on react
when move=comfort fit=neutral
- [Mm. Thanks, I guess.|I know. I just need time.|It's fine, really.]
- [I'll be okay.|It'll pass.|Don't worry about me.]
- [You don't have to say that.|I know you mean well.|That's nice of you.]
- [Hm. Maybe you're right.|We'll see how it goes.|I'll try not to think about it.]
- [{Who} is the one who should be saying that.|I wish {who} would say that.] [But okay.|Thanks, though.]
- [I'll sleep on it.|I'm fine, I just need to not think about it.] [Don't worry so much.|Really.]

@rule react.comfort.neutral.onday
on react
when move=comfort fit=neutral kind=day
- [I know you mean well about {mything}.|It's kind of you, but {mything} won't go away that easily.] [Thanks anyway.|I'll deal with it.]
- [Maybe {mything} will sort itself out.|{Mything} just needs time.] [I hope.|Probably.]
- [It's not as simple as you make {mything} sound.|If only {mything} were that easy.] [But thanks.|I'll be okay.]

@rule react.comfort.bad
on react
when move=comfort fit=bad
