- [{Who} has been good to me, you know.|{Who} isn't a bad person.] [Don't be cruel.|Watch it.]
- [That sounded nastier from you.|When you say it, it sounds so mean.] [Let's stop.|Hm.]

@rule react.agree.bad.onday
on react
when move=agree fit=bad kind=day
feel worried
- [Don't just agree with me about {mything}.|You didn't have to go that far about {mything}.]
- [Now I feel bad for bringing up {mything}.|I wish I hadn't said anything about {mything}.]

@rule react.defend.good
on react
when move=defend fit=good
feel smile
- [You're right. I shouldn't talk like that about {who}.|That's kind of you.|Yeah... {who} doesn't deserve that.]
- [That's nice of you to say.|You're a good person, you know.|Okay, I'll stop.]
- [Mm. {who} is nice, actually.|I guess I got carried away.|Fair point.]
- [I like that you stood up for {who}.|You're right. It's just gossip.|Yeah. Let's leave {who} alone.]
- [You're right, {who} wouldn't do that on purpose.|Knowing {who}, there's probably a reason.] [I got carried away.|Thanks.]
- [I shouldn't spread things about {who}.|I didn't think about how {who} would feel.] [I'm sorry.|You're right.]
- [It's nice that you stick up for people.|You don't even have to do that for {who}.] [I like that about you.|Thanks.]
- [Maybe I'll go talk to {who} directly.|I should ask {who} myself.] [That's fairer.|Good idea.]
- [If people said that about me, I'd want you around.|I hope you'd do the same for me.] [Hehe.|Would you?]

@rule react.defend.neutral
on react
when move=defend fit=neutral
